  "scope": "Complete product request admission composes full frame validation before cold successor authority, native canonical identity, operation and exact budget correspondence. The real VM supplies unchanged limits/hooks and maps payload-free Frame/Correspondence provenance to the original faults; both current and legacy request decoders retain this gate. A VM-free parsed-source consumer uses the same complete entry for original and bounded wire-restored atomic and Seq/All requests, with unchanged output, preparation and every fuel cutoff. Twelve torn source frames refuse before request identity. Frozen frame and request gates retain 24,570 operation and 1,680 cold-authority comparisons and add 4,200 conflicting frame/request cases including checked decoding. Opaque local owners require no Clone, Debug, serde, equality or thread traits; ordered owner/token/sequence hooks borrow original data, skip later work on refusal, drop unused captures and propagate each native unwind without retry. Preflighted correspondence remains available only after frame admission. Mutable/decoded data must be rechecked; consistent exhausted budgets are not grants. Ingress/pending payload bounds, canonical restore admission, authentic authority/original budgets, current deadlines, receipts, leases and atomic settlement remain native. No new evaluator, codec, allocator, meter, wire/journal schema or independent durable VM/extraction promotion.",
